The aggregations over a window whose code Dense_Agg_Code.thy refines: MIN, MAX
and MED keep an order-statistic tree per group, which the sliding window both
inserts into and deletes from (with repeated values, and with deletions at
inner nodes of the single-group trees); MIN and MAX are read off the ends of
the tree; and every aggregation's result table is built from a sorted list.
Integer and string values, grouped and ungrouped.  The expected output was
recorded from the verified monitor before the change and agrees with MonPoly's
on every formula.

  $ while IFS= read -r phi; do
  >   [ -z "$phi" ] && continue
  >   printf '%s\n' "$phi" > f.mfotl
  >   echo "=== $phi"
  >   verimon -sig rank.sig -formula f.mfotl -log rank.log 2>&1
  > done < formulas.txt
